  "chapter": 806,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 89 Chapter 806\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8442, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to requiring\n        that applications submitted by  individuals  with  developmental\n        disabilities for eligibility determinations and service authori-\n        zations be processed in a timely manner\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  legislation would amend the Mental Hygiene Law to require eligi-\nbility determination and service authorization applications for individ-\nuals with intellectual and developmental disabilities to be completed by\nthe Office for People With Developmental Disabilities (OPWDD) within 120\ndays, except in cases where applications  are  unclear,  incomplete,  or\nsubmitted fraudulently.\n\n  I fully support the intent of this legislation. With the ever-increas-\ning demand for services, it is imperative that individuals receive time-\nly  consideration and determination of eligibility. Due to the important\nnature of these services for individuals with intellectual and  develop-\nmental  disabilities to live more independent and fulfilling lives, this\nlegislation  will  prevent  unnecessary  delays  in  receipt  of   those\nservices.\n \n  However,  changes  to this bill were necessary to streamline reporting\nrequirements to advance the underlying intention of  providing  services\nquickly.  Additionally,  as drafted, the bill created two parallel time-\nlines for processing applications, which would create inconsistency  and\nconfusion.  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to make the\nnecessary changes and, with those secured, I am  pleased  to  sign  this\nbill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
